BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Crystal Cross
DTSTART:20260515T193000Z
DTEND:20260515T211000Z
DTSTAMP:20260515T193000Z
UID:sPAQccmQrv
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 88 mins (1h28m)\n\nA quirky Christian singer and a s
 uicidal loner road trip across America\, forging an unlikely bond. Crystal
  Cross is a tender\, offbeat meditation on faith\, fracture\, and unexpect
 ed connection\, enveloped in an excellent soundtrack.Director Richie Jame
 s Follin (Cherokee) scheduled to attend.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/
 crystal-cross\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • Uptown House 3 (Thu 14 May\, 8:00
  PM)\n\nEstimated start: 12:40
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Valentina
DTSTART:20260515T220000Z
DTEND:20260515T234500Z
DTSTAMP:20260515T220000Z
UID:94W6nAfwo5
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 92 mins (1h32m)\n\nIn this humorous docu-comedy\, Ke
 yla Monterrose Mejia shines as the titular character Valentina\, a beleagu
 ered El Paso resident confronting city council in her campaign for local e
 conomic justice. Director Tatti Ribeiro scheduled to attend.\n\nhttps://ww
 w.siff.net/festival/valentina\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • Uptown House 3 (T
 hu 14 May\, 5:30 PM)\n\nEstimated start: 15:10
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Roid
DTSTART:20260516T003000Z
DTEND:20260516T023000Z
DTSTAMP:20260516T003000Z
UID:Nsru4AfYD0
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 109 mins (1h49m)\n\nEach time Shadhu tries to leave 
 his wife behind\, a fruit drops from the palm tree\, and she finds her way
  back. Mejbaur Rahman Sumon’s Roid is part folk tale\, fable\, and somet
 hing harder to name.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/roid\n\nAlso playing
  at:\n  • Film Center (Sat 16 May\, 2:30 PM)\n\nEstimated start: 17:40
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:EIGHT BRIDGES
DTSTART:20260516T033000Z
DTEND:20260516T050500Z
DTSTAMP:20260516T033000Z
UID:UfZNjVJSoV
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 82 mins (1h22m)\n\nThere is something hypnotically a
 lluring about James Benning’s work. With only eight shots\, each of a di
 fferent bridge\, it’s like taking more than a cursory look at a gallery 
 painting: the longer you look\, the deeper you see.\n\nhttps://www.siff.ne
 t/festival/eight-bridges\n\nEstimated start: 20:40
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Reality Check
DTSTART:20260516T190000Z
DTEND:20260516T204500Z
DTSTAMP:20260516T190000Z
UID:unLWAa9Hpg
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 93 mins (1h33m)\n\nThese inventive and enlightening 
 nonfiction shorts highlight the quiet—and in one case quite loud—ways 
 that people assert their dignity in times of war\, disaster\, division\, a
 nd competitive burping.Filmmakers scheduled to attend.\n\nhttps://www.siff
 .net/festival/reality-check\n\nEstimated start: 12:10
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
